Z||000009||wilburt||04-03-2001||09:59 PM||||Mr.Frosty, I live in Edwardsville IL right now, but I drive to, and work everyday in Troy, Mo. Yeah, I-70 is in bad shape! Not much chance of being passed by that green thing there. Where are you? I'd love to see a formula T-top.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mr.Frosty||04-04-2001||10:15 AM||||As far as times go I havn't had it track side<BR>for testing,but it can win stoplight races with most tuned imports and v8 muscle cars,and that's only straight line racing.I can't wait to get my 17" inch rims for it for summer.Wilburt,I live off of the St.Charles rock road near I-170,but my Mom lives in St.Peters off of Mid rivers mall dr.,so I drive that way a few times a week.I keep the 85Gt there in the garage as it's a little nicer than the Formula.It hasn't seen a rainy day in 6 years.My formula on the other hand has been a daily driver since I got it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Oh well,I'm going to fix it up eventually too.I've done a lot of work to it though.I've replaced most of the mechanical,suspension,cooling parts on the car.The engine is at 126,xxx,but it doesn't smoke or use much oil.The tranny is strong too.It's got nice 16" OZ rims also with fat tires.I need to lower it sometime in the future.The only thing that sucks about t-tops is "water" and lots of it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||6
